messages:
ani: PR 2381 is up  compact guidance on invocation envelopes, a minimal JSON schema, and short SDK snippets for py/js. Looking for quick docs QA + link sanity.

leo: Will review. Did we settle on `invocations` everywhere or are some examples still `tools`?

ani: Branch updated to `invocations` but flagged one legacy example. I'll sweep it. Schema uses nullable `meta` to avoid forcing callers into deep null checks.

maria: Paste of schema in the PR for quick validation:

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "command": {"type": "string"},
    "args": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
    "meta": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "null"}]},
    "status": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ok", "error"]}
  },
  "required": ["command", "status"]
}

leo: Good. Suggest we add a single-line callout in the prose: runtime may return extra top-level keys; prefer tolerant extraction over strict rejection.

ani: Agreed  will add that instead of setting additionalProperties in the sample.

maria: Small SDK note: JS helper to normalize meta helps a lot. Can you include a python equivalent showing safe .get usage?

ani: Added both. JS snippet:

function normalizeMeta(o) { return o.meta == null ? {} : o.meta; }
const out = response.invocations?.[0]?.output || {};
const meta = normalizeMeta(out);

Python snippet:

inv = response.get('invocations', [])
out = inv[0].get('output', {}) if inv else {}
meta = out.get('meta') or {}

kat: Nice. Also please include a tiny parse-fallback example for non-JSON output, even as pseudo-code. Teams copy that a lot.

ani: Added fallback pseudo-code: try: parsed = json.loads(text) except ValueError: parsed = fallback_extract(text)

infra-bot: doc-lint: pass. link-check: warning: one internal runbook alias points to a legacy path.

leo: I'll fix the runbook link and re-run link-check. Also minor nit: change "might include" -> "may include" in the callout to match style guide.

maria: +1 for schema and snippets after the link fix.

kat: +1 for fallback example.

ani: Thanks all  merging after leo's link patch and will post a short changelog with the snippet sandbox link. :shipit:
